---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import { company } from '../../data/site';

const effective = 'November 26, 2026';
const email = company.email;
---

<Base
  title="DocScan Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for DocScan, the offline document scanner app published by EnerBate Solutions Inc. The app collects no personal data."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="DocScan"
    title="Privacy policy"
    lede="DocScan is a document scanner for Android and iPhone that works entirely on your device. In short: we do not collect, store or share any personal data."
    crumbs={[{ href: '/', label: 'Home' }]}
  />

  <section class="wrap py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="prose-b max-w-3xl text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed">
      <p class="text-sm">
        Effective date: {effective} · Publisher: {company.name}, Canada · Contact:{' '}<a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
      </p>

      <h3>What we collect</h3>
      <p>
        Nothing. DocScan never connects to the internet (on Android it does not
        even have the internet permission). It has no user accounts, no
        advertising and no analytics or tracking tools. We, {company.name}, never
        receive your documents, photos, recognized text or any information about
        how you use the app.
      </p>

      <h3>Your documents stay on your device</h3>
      <p>
        Scans, recognized text (OCR), signatures, notes and settings are stored
        only in the app's private storage on your phone. They leave your device
        only when you choose to do so, for example when you share, print, save a
        file to a folder, or create a backup. Where that file goes is decided by
        you and by the app you send it to.
      </p>

      <h3>Permissions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Camera</strong>: to scan documents and QR codes. Images are processed on the device.</li>
        <li><strong>Photos</strong> (iPhone): to pick the pictures you want to turn into documents, and to save scans to the "DocScan" album when you ask for it. The app sees only the pictures you pick.</li>
        <li><strong>Fingerprint, Face ID / biometrics</strong>: only if you turn on the app lock or locked folders. The check is done by Android or iOS; the app never sees your fingerprint or face.</li>
        <li><strong>Storage</strong> (older Android versions only): to import and save files you choose.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Services provided by Google or Apple on your device</h3>
      <p>On Android:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Document scanner</strong>: the automatic page scanner is
          provided by Google Play services (ML Kit) and runs on the device.
          Google's own <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">privacy policy</a>{' '}applies to Google Play services.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Optional contributions</strong>: if you choose to contribute,
          the payment is handled entirely by Google Play. EnerBate gives the net
          proceeds to orphans, people in need, stranded travellers and refugees.
          We receive no payment card details; Google Play's terms and privacy
          policy apply.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>On iPhone:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Document scanner and ID photos</strong>: the automatic page
          scanner and the person detection for ID photos are provided by iOS
          (Apple's VisionKit and Vision) and run on the device.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Optional contributions</strong>: if you choose to contribute,
          the payment is handled entirely by the App Store. The net proceeds are
          used in the same way. We receive no payment card details; Apple's
          terms and <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">privacy policy</a>{' '}apply.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Backups</h3>
      <p>
        Android's automatic cloud backup stays off for DocScan: nothing is sent
        to Google's backup servers. When you move to a new phone directly (by
        cable or Wi-Fi, "copy apps and data"), your documents and settings are
        copied to the new phone.
      </p>
      <p>
        The app's own backup creates a file only when you ask for it, and you
        choose where to keep it. If you turn on <em>Automatic backup</em>,
        DocScan keeps one backup file up to date in the place you chose, for
        example Google Drive. DocScan itself still never connects to the
        internet: the app that owns that place (such as Google Drive) stores and
        uploads the file, under that service's terms. You can turn it off at any
        time in Settings.
      </p>
      <p>
        On iPhone, DocScan keeps its documents out of your iPhone's iCloud or
        computer backup. If you turn on <em>Include documents in iPhone backup</em>{' '}in
        Settings, iOS includes them when it backs up your iPhone; Apple then
        stores that backup under its own terms. You can turn it off again at any
        time. <em>Automatic backup</em> is available on Android only.
      </p>

      <h3>Children</h3>
      <p>
        DocScan is a general-purpose utility and does not knowingly collect any
        information from anyone, including children.
      </p>

      <h3>Changes and contact</h3>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the new version will be published on this page
        with a new effective date. Questions: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

  </section>
</Base>
